{"id": "EUVD-2026-81109", "enisaUuid": "ce6d9cd6-7410-3f06-83af-4abac569956c", "description": "A vulnerability in the External Database Access feature of Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC) Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to execute arbitrary commands as&nbsp;root on an affected device.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to insecure deserialization of a user-supplied Java byte stream from a host that is configured in the external database access list. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted, serialized Java byte stream to a specific TCP port of an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to execute arbitrary commands on the device and elevate privileges to root.\r\nNotes:\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability can be exploited only by an attacker who has control of a host in the external database access list.\r\nIf the FMC management interface does not have public internet access, the attack surface that is associated with this vulnerability is reduced.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:08:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T03:55:57", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-fmc-javarce-y2NypXwk"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mgpv-rwhr-9mx2", "CVE-2026-20242"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01185437-6b99-3fcf-9342-71a33e0586e5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.6.3"}, {"id": "02e7a035-6e1e-39f1-bef0-38d1f14c7a75", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.6.2.1"}, {"id": "05c42ad9-48d3-3dab-97ae-9a7be517fe3a", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.2.10.2"}, {"id"